  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "05. Attack Sequence",
    "ruleNumber": "05.04",
    "summary": "The opposing player resolves each **save roll** in turn, lowest result first, until every attack is resolved or the whole target unit is **destroyed**; any attacks left over are then lost. For each roll:\n\n1. Select Model: from the current allocation group (05.04.01), pick a wounded model if there is one.\n2. Check Save Roll: the first matching case below applies.\n3. Resolve Damage: on damage, the model loses wounds equal to the attack's D and is destroyed at 0 or fewer remaining wounds.\n\nThe save roll cases, in order:\n\n- an unmodified 1 inflicts damage\n- a roll at or above the group's InSv fails\n- a roll at or above the model's Sv after applying the weapon's AP fails\n- anything else inflicts damage\n\nA model a rule lets attack after it is destroyed, such as one that fights immediately after its attacker, follows Fight On Death (05.04.05).",
